{"name":"Lavender Rose","hex":"#fba0e3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lavender","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a group of European plants, genus, Lavandula, of the mint family.","A pale bluish purple or violet colour, like that of the lavender flower."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour.","Pertaining to LGBT people and rights."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lavender"},{"term":"rose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub of the genus Rosa, with red, pink, white or yellow flowers.","A flower of the rose plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make rose-colored; to redden or flush.","To perfume, as with roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lavandula","blocks":[{"text":"Lavandula is a genus of 47 known species of perennial flowering plants in the sage family, Lamiaceae. It is native to regions of the Iberian Peninsula and Mediterranean coastline, the Middle East, extending to the Indian subcontinent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Single_lavender_flower02.jpg/330px-Single_lavender_flower02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavandula","wikidata":"Q171892"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose","wikidata":"Q34687"},{"title":"Lavender (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lavender is a light shade of purple or violet. It applies particularly to the color of the flower of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Lavandula_fields.jpg/330px-Lavandula_fields.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavender_(color)","wikidata":"Q2468392"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg/330px-Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_(color)","wikidata":"Q533047"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/A_small_white_feeding_on_a_lavender_flower.jpg/500px-A_small_white_feeding_on_a_lavender_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/A_small_white_feeding_on_a_lavender_flower.jpg/1280px-A_small_white_feeding_on_a_lavender_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/A_small_white_feeding_on_a_lavender_flower.jpg/500px-A_small_white_feeding_on_a_lavender_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A lavender serving as a nectar source for a small white butterfly","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_small_white_feeding_on_a_lavender_flower.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Hitchin_lavender_fields.jpg/500px-Hitchin